Game of Life on sparse tiles (benchmarks/life/life-sparse.m) in a GPU
process on the machine's GPU: a team steps each active tile, its threads
over the tile's cells, and the process's lane does the bookkeeping. The
population and checksum are the dense programs' for the same world
(life-sparse.test), with the default world too, 8192 cells square, a soup
of 256 and 1000 steps, which only some 45 tiles cover.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/life/life-sparse.m -o %t
RUN: %gpu-env LIFE_WORLD=256 LIFE_TILE=16 LIFE_SOUP=64 LIFE_STEPS=50 timeout -k 1 60 %t | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=A
A: Population: 562
A-NEXT: Checksum: 17668223
A-NEXT: Active tiles: 36 at most, 32 at the end
RUN: %gpu-env LIFE_WORLD=200 LIFE_TILE=8 LIFE_SOUP=37 LIFE_STEPS=120 timeout -k 1 60 %t | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ODD
ODD: Population: 157
ODD-NEXT: Checksum: 2963654
RUN: %gpu-env LIFE_WORLD=256 LIFE_TILE=8 LIFE_SOUP=256 LIFE_STEPS=100 timeout -k 1 60 %t | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WHOLE
WHOLE: Population: 4947
WHOLE-NEXT: Checksum: 158368224
RUN: %gpu-env timeout -k 1 60 %t | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DEFAULT
DEFAULT: World: 8192 x 8192 cells, tiles of 64 x 64, 8192 in the pool
DEFAULT: Population: 3719
DEFAULT-NEXT: Checksum: 124925383998

Without -fopenmp the process runs the loops on its own lane.
RUN: merkc -O2 -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/life/life-sparse.m -o %t.sequential
RUN: %gpu-env LIFE_WORLD=256 LIFE_TILE=16 LIFE_SOUP=64 LIFE_STEPS=50 timeout -k 1 60 %t.sequential | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=A
